From: Eric Tanner <eric.tanner@harvia.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: vt-sbc-am62l: A53 cpufreq through the SCMI clock

The A53s run at a flat 1.25 GHz from reset to shutdown: the stock DT has no
OPP table, the SCMI firmware exposes no perf domain, and ti-cpufreq knows
nothing about AM62L3 in this tree. Both cores at full clock for the whole
8 s boot is the bulk of the start-up current peak.

Upstream (January 2026, "arm64: dts: ti: k3-am62l: support cpufreq") drives
the cluster clock through SCMI clock 356 with a 200 MHz - 1.25 GHz OPP
table (600 MHz floor here, see the DT comment). This does the same with a
plain operating-points-v2 table so that cpufreq-dt (already =y) picks it up
without ti-cpufreq. With cpufreq.default_governor=ondemand (U-Boot optargs)
the boot still runs at the top OPP under load and the idle app drops to
600 MHz. Verified on the bench board: Vantron's DM firmware (inside its
tispl.bin) accepts the rate change on clock 356 and scaling_cur_freq
follows the governor.
Enabled from site.conf with
  SRC_URI:append:pn-linux-ti-staging = " file://vt-sbc-am62l-a53-cpufreq-via-scmi.patch"

Signed-off-by: Eric Tanner <eric.tanner@harvia.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/ti/vt-sbc-am62l.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/ti/vt-sbc-am62l.dtsi
@@ -242,6 +242,49 @@
 			gpios = <&main_gpio0 36 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 		};
 	};
+
+	/*
+	 * A53 operating points, driven through the SCMI clock protocol the
+	 * DM firmware already exposes (clock 356 is the compute cluster's A53
+	 * clock in TI's AM62L clock table; the same ID upstream uses in
+	 * "arm64: dts: ti: k3-am62l: support cpufreq"). Plain
+	 * operating-points-v2 rather than the -ti-cpu variant: there is no
+	 * ti-cpufreq AM62L3 support in this 6.12 tree, and this part is
+	 * running at 1.25 GHz so every step below it is safe. VDD_CORE stays
+	 * at its fixed 0.75 V (no DVS on this PMIC rail), so this is DFS only.
+	 */
+	a53_opp_table: opp-table {
+		compatible = "operating-points-v2";
+		opp-shared;
+
+		opp-600000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <600000000>;
+			clock-latency-ns = <6000000>;
+		};
+		opp-800000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <800000000>;
+			clock-latency-ns = <6000000>;
+		};
+		opp-1000000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <1000000000>;
+			clock-latency-ns = <6000000>;
+		};
+		opp-1250000000 {
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <1250000000>;
+			clock-latency-ns = <6000000>;
+			opp-suspend;
+		};
+	};
+};
+
+&cpu0 {
+	clocks = <&scmi_clk 356>;
+	operating-points-v2 = <&a53_opp_table>;
+};
+
+&cpu1 {
+	clocks = <&scmi_clk 356>;
+	operating-points-v2 = <&a53_opp_table>;
 };
 
 &main_gpio0 {
